          %h1#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Euclidean supermanifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            that can be thought of as being equipped with a flat
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
          %p
            Alternatively, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            for which the transition functions of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} atlas
            are restricted to be elements of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Euclidean+group"} super Euclidean group
          %h1#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Euclidean supermanifold
            of dimension
            = succeed "is" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p|q)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            that is quipped with an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
